    <node id="&quot;243-YEAR CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 243-year cycle refers to the periodicity of the transits of Venus, with each pair of transits occurring approximately 8 years apart, followed by gaps of 121.5 and 105.5 years."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNODIC PERIODS OF VENUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A synodic period of Venus is the time it takes for Venus to return to the same position relative to the Sun as seen from Earth, which is approximately 584 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;152 SYNODIC PERIODS OF VENUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"152 synodic periods of Venus correspond to the 243-year cycle of the transits of Venus."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6</data>
    </node>
